<Base title="About" description="Platform engineer & solutions architect.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm Waleed — a platform engineer and solutions architect. For about a decade I've been building,
      shipping, and selling Kubernetes infrastructure at scale: multi-cluster load balancing, node
      lifecycle, GitOps delivery, and the full path from architecture to production for enterprise
      customers.
    </p>
    <p>
      I create and maintain open-source infrastructure tooling — most actively <a
        href="https://github.com/kubermatic/kubelb">KubeLB</a
      >, a centralized load-balancing platform for multi-cluster Kubernetes. These days a lot of my
      attention is on self-hosted LLM platforms: GPU substrate, inference-aware routing, and the real
      economics of running models yourself.
    </p>
    <p>This site is where I write that down. No newsletter, no tracking — just notes and links.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
